# SETTINGS

Settings must be organized, searchable, documented, defaulted, and resettable.

## Requirements

| Area | Rule |
|---|---|
| Categories | Group panels under Account / Business / Communications / Safety / Appearance (`settingsCatalog.js`) |
| Searchable | In-page search filters panels + options; global search indexes the same catalog |
| Documented | Every panel and preference has `description` + `docs` (what it does / default) |
| Defaults | Explicit defaults for notifications, privacy, marketing, appearance |
| Reset | Preference panels expose **Restore defaults** (not profile/password/accounts) |

## Architecture

- Catalog: `src/lib/settingsCatalog.js`
- UI: `src/pages/Settings.jsx`
- Do not invent settings outside the catalog without documenting defaults

## Honesty

- Reset does not erase profile, company, password, or OAuth links  
- Device appearance applies immediately; remote `theme_pref` saves on Save  

## Definition of done

Incomplete if Settings is a flat unsearchable list, options lack docs/defaults, or preference panels cannot restore defaults.
